  "raw_text_summary": "To transform a 1-hour Zoom recording into five engaging LinkedIn video clips, a structured workflow involving transcription, intelligent clipping, editing, and adherence to LinkedIn's video specifications is recommended. Leading tools, many leveraging AI, can significantly streamline this process.\n\nHere's a step-by-step guide:\n\n### 1. Download Your Zoom Recording\n\nFirst, obtain the video file from Zoom.\n*   **Zoom Cloud Recordings:** Sign in to the Zoom web portal, navigate to \"Recordings,\" select \"Cloud Recordings,\" open the desired recording, and click \"Download\" to get the MP4 file.\n*   **Local Recordings:** If you recorded locally, the MP4 file will be in a Zoom folder on your computer, typically in `Documents/Zoom` on Windows or `/Users/[Username]/Documents/Zoom` on a Mac.\n\n### 2. Identify Key Moments and Transcribe\n\nA 1-hour recording needs to be condensed into impactful, short clips (ideally 30-90 seconds for awareness content, up to 15 minutes for longer posts). Transcription is crucial for this step and for adding captions later.\n\n**Leading Tools for AI Clipping & Transcription:**\nMany AI-powered tools can automatically transcribe your video, identify highlights, and even suggest clips.\n*   **OpusClip:** Uses AI to detect key moments, trim long videos, add captions, and reframe clips for various platforms (e.g., 9:16 for vertical, 1:1 or 4:5 for feeds, 16:9 for landscape). It also provides a \"Virality Score.\"\n*   **Klap:** An AI clipper that automatically selects clips.\n*   **Vizard:** Offers AI-powered transcription and an editor to repurpose content into viral clips, allowing adjustments to aspect ratio, cropping, and captions.\n*   **Descript:** Excellent for turning interviews, webinars, and podcasts into clips by editing the text of the transcript.\n*   **CapCut:** While known for mobile editing, its desktop version offers AI-assisted clipping, auto-captions, and templates for short-form content.\n*   **Pictory:** Upload a long video, podcast, or webinar, and Pictory generates short videos, summaries, clips, and highlights.\n*   **Choppity:** An AI tool that transcribes, finds standalone short-form content moments, trims, reframes to 9:16, and adds animated captions.\n*   **LumiClip",
